From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orangepi6 kernel-7 port
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT sched fair account misfit load as 6.18 did

On 7.3.5 one or two of eight busy threads stay on the little cores
(capacity 279) while a big core is idle, costing ~12% on llama.cpp.
6.18 places them on the big cores. EAS, LLC balancing, the governor and
the NI_* newidle features are ruled out on the board. One 7.x change in
update_sg_lb_stats() only accounts a group's misfit load when dst_cpu's
capacity is greater than the group's max_capacity. Go back to the 6.18
accounting to test whether that change is what keeps the threads on the
little cores.
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 913630c0b..dbfcbadef 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -12308,14 +12308,15 @@ static inline void update_sg_lb_stats(struct lb_env *env,
 					*sg_overloaded = 1;
 
 				/*
-				 * Only account misfit load if @dst_cpu can
-				 * help; otherwise, the group may be classified
-				 * as misfit_task and update_sd_pick_busiest()
-				 * will skip it.
+				 * Sky1: account misfit load whatever @dst_cpu is,
+				 * as 6.18 did. With the "only if @dst_cpu can
+				 * help" test from 7.x, threads stayed on the
+				 * little cores (capacity 279) while a big core
+				 * sat idle: the group's max_capacity is not a
+				 * good proxy on this five-level capacity
+				 * topology.
 				 */
-				if (capacity_greater(capacity_of(env->dst_cpu),
-						     group->sgc->max_capacity) &&
-				    (sgs->group_misfit_task_load < rq->misfit_task_load))
+				if (sgs->group_misfit_task_load < rq->misfit_task_load)
 					sgs->group_misfit_task_load = rq->misfit_task_load;
 			}
 		} else if (env->idle && sched_reduced_capacity(rq, env->sd)) {
